From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ad5x: Log detail row (Klipper's LOG_MODE); screen log level
 follows it

Settings > System gets "Log detail: Short / Extended" when Klipper has
Kiln's ad5x_log object; it sends LOG_MODE MODE=short|extended and shows
printer.ad5x_log.mode. HelixScreen's own Log Level row is hidden then.
Ad5xLogModel follows the object from discovery on (as the auto-refill
model) and sets this screen's log level at once: warn in short mode,
debug in extended, also when the mode changes from the console or
LOG_MODE's HOURS run out. S70helixscreen sets the start level from the
same mode. Strings in en and ru.
